1
00:00:00,729 --> 00:00:03,729
Let's look at the number n!

2
00:00:04,179 --> 00:00:06,379
and try to factor it.

3
00:00:06,829 --> 00:00:09,629
How many times does 2 appear in it?

4
00:00:10,079 --> 00:00:11,879
That's fairly easy:

5
00:00:12,329 --> 00:00:14,929
once for every even number up to n,

6
00:00:15,179 --> 00:00:18,579
once more for every number divisible by 4,

7
00:00:19,029 --> 00:00:20,829
and so on.

8
00:00:21,279 --> 00:00:23,879
What about 3? It's similar,

9
00:00:24,129 --> 00:00:26,729
and so on for all the primes up to n.

10
00:00:27,179 --> 00:00:29,379
Writing it this way is cumbersome,

11
00:00:29,629 --> 00:00:32,229
so we'll use product and sum notation.

